{"title":"CraneParcel","sub":"One parcel in eight needs a second trip","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Parcel delivery","geo":"United States","diff":1,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Last-mile economics · option comparison","prompt":"CraneParcel delivers 30 million parcels a year for online retailers in the Northeast. About 12% of first delivery attempts fail because nobody is home, and each redelivery costs about $6. The operations director has two ideas: text customers a one-hour delivery window, or install parcel lockers. Which should come first?","clarify":[{"q":"Delivery windows?","a":"Customers get a text with a one-hour window and can redirect the parcel. In a trial, failures fell to 7%. Texts and tracking cost about $0.05 a parcel."},{"q":"Lockers?","a":"1,500 lockers at $8k each to install and $1.2k a year to run. About 8% of parcels would go to lockers. Only 1% of locker deliveries fail, and dropping many parcels at one locker saves about $1.20 a parcel."},{"q":"Can both be done?","a":"Yes; budget is the constraint this year."}],"structure":{"root":"How should CraneParcel cut failed deliveries?","branches":[{"head":"Size of the problem","items":["Failures × redelivery cost"]},{"head":"Delivery windows","items":["Failures avoided","Cost per parcel"]},{"head":"Lockers","items":["Failures avoided","Cheaper drops","Investment"]}]},"hypothesis":"Windows apply to every parcel at almost no cost, so they probably save the most quickly. Lockers need investment and only reach a small share of parcels.","questions":[{"q":"How much do failed deliveries cost today?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>30M × 12% = 3.6M redeliveries × $6 = <b>$21.6M a year</b>.</p>"},{"q":"Compare the two ideas.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"388.459719pt\" height=\"158.164pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 388.459719 158.164\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-line