25173 16.896 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pccd0138051)\" style=\"fill: #c2410c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_4\"><path d=\"M 225.752446 133.056 L 365.534264 133.056 L 365.534264 91.2384 L 225.752446 91.2384 z\n\" clip-path=\"url(#pccd0138051)\" style=\"fill: #0a8f9c\"/></g><g id=\"patch_5\"><path d=\"M 35.299719 133.056 L 35.299719 11.088 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"patch_6\"><path d=\"M 35.299719 133.056 L 381.259719 133.056 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_8\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(115.067332 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" d=\"M 3456 4749 Q 3507 4749 3532 4723 Q 3558 4698 3552 4672 L 3546 4442 Q 3546 4390 3520 4329 Q 3494 4269 3456 4211 Q 3200 3827 2960 3385 Q 2720 2944 2515 2477 Q 2310 2010 2147 1571 Q 1984 1133 1875 758 Q 1766 384 1728 122 Q 1715 0 1632 0 L 1126 0 Q 1024 0 1050 109 Q 1139 467 1289 918 Q 1440 1370 1661 1891 Q 1882 2413 2182 2982 Q 2483 3552 2861 4147 Q 2886 4186 2880 4211 Q 2874 4237 2816 4237 L 339 4237 Q 262 4237 262 4314 L 307 4685 Q 314 4749 403 4749 L 3456 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" d=\"M 992 102 Q 992 0 877 0 L 429 0 Q 333 0 333 90 L 333 640 Q 333 723 403 723 L 928 723 Q 992 723 992 646 L 992 102 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" d=\"M 3482 4749 Q 3546 4749 3565 4729 Q 3584 4710 3578 4653 L 3552 4307 Q 3546 4262 3536 4249 Q 3526 4237 3462 4237 L 1286 4237 Q 1210 4237 1210 4166 L 1094 2778 Q 1088 2733 1113 2710 Q 1139 2688 1171 2701 Q 1408 2822 1648 2915 Q 1888 3008 2234 3008 Q 2656 3008 3021 2854 Q 3386 2701 3606 2381 Q 3827 2061 3827 1555 Q 3827 1043 3593 681 Q 3360 320 2947 128 Q 2534 -64 2003 -64 Q 1517 -64 1085 105 Q 653 275 352 602 Q 326 640 323 669 Q 320 698 365 730 L 640 954 Q 691 992 749 934 Q 922 774 1088 652 Q 1254 531 1456 464 Q 1658 397 1926 397 Q 2342 397 2630 544 Q 2918 691 3072 950 Q 3226 1210 3226 1536 Q 3226 1882 3078 2102 Q 2931 2323 2684 2432 Q 2438 2541 2138 2541 Q 1798 2541 1529 2419 Q 1261 2298 1037 2163 Q 986 2138 973 2144 Q 960 2150 922 2170 L 608 2349 Q 550 2381 553 2397 Q 557 2413 563 2490 L 736 4659 Q 742 4717 764 4733 Q 787 4749 877 4749 L 3482 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(80.8125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_9\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(290.014605 89.2704) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-a9\" transform=\"translate(59.90625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-87\" transform=\"translate(80.8125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pccd0138051\"><rect x=\"35.299719\" y=\"11.088\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"121.968\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Yearly saving ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Windows:</b> failures fall 5 points: 30M × 5% × $6 = $9.0M, less 30M × $0.05 = $1.5M: <b>$7.5M a year</b>, no investment.</p> <p><b>Lockers:</b> 8% of parcels = 2.4M; each avoids 11 points of failures (× $6 = $0.66) and saves $1.20 = $1.86 per parcel: $4.46M, less $1.8M running: <b>$2.7M a year</b>, for $12M upfront (payback 4.5 years).</p>"},{"q":"What would you do?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Launch delivery windows across the network now: bigger saving, no investment. Then add lockers in dense areas with the highest failure rates (apartment blocks, offices), where they fill fastest and pay back soonest.</p> <p>Careful: the two savings overlap. Once windows have cut failures to 7%, each locker parcel avoids only 6 points of failure, not 11: 2.4M × (6% × $6 + $1.20) − $1.8M ≈ <b>$1.9M a year</b>, a payback of about 6 years. So put lockers only where failure rates stay high after windows.</p>"}],"reco":"Start with one-hour delivery windows: they cut failures from 12% to about 7% across all 30 million parcels and save about $7.5M a year with no investment. Then roll out lockers in the densest, highest-failure areas: once windows are live, 1,500 lockers would save about $1.9M a year (about $2.7M on their own) for $12M upfront, paying back in about 6 years, so put them first where failures stay highest. Risk: customers ignoring texts. Next step: switch on windows region by region and track failures weekly.","great":["Sizes the problem first","Compares savings and investment for each option","Prioritises the option that reaches every parcel","Targets lockers where they pay back fastest"],"id":87,"slug":"craneparcel"}